# Fake-db stub endpoint rule

The Django app `seopartnerhub/fake_db/` serves the JSON fixtures from
`frontend/full-version/src/fake-db-json/` (mirrored verbatim into
`seopartnerhub/fake_db/data/`) so that `frontend/starter-kit/` can
render UI **before** the corresponding real Django domain endpoint
exists.

## When to use `/api/fake-db/`

Use it **only** when **all** of the following are true:

1. A `starter-kit` component or page needs dynamic data that the
   equivalent `full-version` component reads from
   `src/fake-db-json/<group>/<file>.json` (or its TypeScript twin
   under `src/fake-db/`).
2. There is **no real Django endpoint** for that domain yet (no
   model, no DRF view, no URL).
3. Building the real backend is out of scope for the current task.

Do **not** use it for data that already has a real endpoint
(`/api/users/`, `/_allauth/*`, etc.). Use the real endpoint instead.

## Endpoint surface

The fake-db app exposes exactly two URL patterns under
`/api/fake-db/`:

| Method | URL                              | Returns                                  |
| ------ | -------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| GET    | `/api/fake-db/manifest/`         | `{ "apps": [...], "pages": [...] }`      |
| GET    | `/api/fake-db/<group>/<section>/`| raw JSON from `data/<group>/<section>.json` |

`<group>` MUST be `apps` or `pages` (matches the on-disk layout and
the `frontend/full-version/src/fake-db-json/` layout). `<section>` is
the JSON filename without extension (e.g. `userProfile`, `academy`).

All fake-db endpoints require `IsAuthenticated`.

OpenAPI: every fake-db view is tagged `fake-db (stub)` and the
description starts with `STUB DATA.` — this groups them in Swagger
and makes them trivial to find/remove.

## Backend conventions

When **adding** a new fake-db fixture:

1. Drop a `*.json` file under `seopartnerhub/fake_db/data/apps/` or
   `seopartnerhub/fake_db/data/pages/`. Filename must match the
   `frontend/full-version/src/fake-db-json/<group>/<file>.json` it
   mirrors. **Never** hand-author the JSON: copy it from
   `frontend/full-version/src/fake-db-json/`. That folder is the
   source of truth; the Django copy is a mirror.
2. No code change is required — `FakeDbSectionLoader` picks new files
   up automatically.
3. Do not add new HTTP routes; everything goes through
   `FakeDbSectionView`.

Every public symbol in `seopartnerhub/fake_db/` MUST start its
docstring with `STUB.` or `STUB DATA` so the intent is unambiguous in
code search.

## Frontend conventions (starter-kit)

When **consuming** fake-db data in `frontend/starter-kit/`:

1. All fake-db calls go through helpers under
   `frontend/starter-kit/src/lib/fakeDb/` (e.g. a thin wrapper around
   `apiRequest('/api/fake-db/<group>/<section>/')`).
   No component, view, or page may call `fetch('/api/fake-db/...')`
   directly.
2. Mark every call site with a short comment:

   ```ts
   // STUB: /api/fake-db/. Replace with the real `<domain>` endpoint when implemented.
   ```

3. Do **not** copy `src/fake-db/`, `src/fake-db-json/`, or
   `src/app/api/*` mock routes from `frontend/full-version/` into
   `frontend/starter-kit/`. The starter-kit must always go through
   Django.

## Migrating off a fake-db endpoint

When a real Django domain endpoint for a section is implemented:

1. Build the real DRF endpoint with the field shape that the
   `frontend/full-version` mock already exposes (frontend-first
   contract — see `frontend-parity.mdc`).
2. Update the starter-kit caller in `src/lib/fakeDb/` (or move it
   out of `fakeDb/` entirely) to point to the new endpoint, and
   remove the `STUB:` comment.
3. Delete the now-unused `seopartnerhub/fake_db/data/<group>/<section>.json`
   if no other component still uses it.

## Forbidden

- Adding business logic, models, migrations, or Celery tasks inside
  `seopartnerhub/fake_db/`. The app is a passive file server.
- Mutating fake-db JSON in tests or at runtime — fixtures are
  read-only.
- Calling `/api/fake-db/` from server code other than
  `starter-kit`'s `src/lib/fakeDb/` helpers.
- Authoring new JSON directly in `seopartnerhub/fake_db/data/`
  instead of mirroring it from `frontend/full-version/src/fake-db-json/`.
